From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alan Bradburne <abradburne@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 22:06:45 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] mfd: rk8xx: skip SLPPIN_DN_FUN and wait for DEV_OFF on
 power-off

When an RK809 or RK817 has system-power-controller, rk808_power_off()
powers the board off directly via DEV_OFF in RK817_SYS_CFG(3). Two
things in the upstream shutdown path interfere with that:

- rk8xx_shutdown() writes SLPPIN_DN_FUN to RK817_SYS_CFG(3) immediately
  before do_kernel_power_off_prepare() writes DEV_OFF to the same
  register, arming the SLEEP pin for power-down and issuing back-to-back
  writes to 0xf4.
- rk808_power_off() returns NOTIFY_DONE immediately after writing
  DEV_OFF, letting kernel_power_off() continue into syscore_shutdown()
  and PSCI/TF-A before the PMIC finishes cutting power.

Skip arming SLPPIN_DN_FUN in rk8xx_shutdown() when the PMIC is the
system power controller, and wait 100 ms in rk808_power_off() after a
successful DEV_OFF write so the PMIC completes power-off cleanly.

Upstream status: candidate.
---
 drivers/mfd/rk8xx-core.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/mfd/rk8xx-core.c b/drivers/mfd/rk8xx-core.c
index 3dcf6ab..0cccfa9 100644
--- a/drivers/mfd/rk8xx-core.c
+++ b/drivers/mfd/rk8xx-core.c
@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@
  */
 
 #include <linux/bitfield.h>
+#include <linux/delay.h>
 #include <linux/interrupt.h>
 #include <linux/mfd/rk808.h>
 #include <linux/mfd/core.h>
@@ -706,6 +707,8 @@ static int rk808_power_off(struct sys_off_data *data)
 	ret = regmap_update_bits(rk808->regmap, reg, bit, bit);
 	if (ret)
 		dev_err(rk808->dev, "Failed to shutdown device!\n");
+	else
+		mdelay(100);
 
 	return NOTIFY_DONE;
 }
@@ -747,6 +750,15 @@ void rk8xx_shutdown(struct device *dev)
 		break;
 	case RK809_ID:
 	case RK817_ID:
+		/*
+		 * When the PMIC is the system power controller, rk808_power_off()
+		 * cuts power via DEV_OFF in RK817_SYS_CFG(3). Writing
+		 * SLPPIN_DN_FUN to the same register immediately before DEV_OFF
+		 * is unnecessary and arms the SLEEP pin for power-down.
+		 */
+		if (device_property_read_bool(dev, "system-power-controller") ||
+		    device_property_read_bool(dev, "rockchip,system-power-controller"))
+			return;
 		ret = regmap_update_bits(rk808->regmap,
 					 RK817_SYS_CFG(3),
 					 RK817_SLPPIN_FUNC_MSK,
